title: treeref:find
tags: [[GUI command]] [[TreeRef forest]]
kind: reference
summary: TreeRef explorer: jump to a child by name

Moves the cursor of the [[treeref panel]] to a child named in the command input, among those loaded ([[Jumping to an entry]]).

The first argument is the mode. `treeref:find select` (<<key "treeref:find select" f>>) selects the child without going into it. `treeref:find walk` (<<key "treeref:find walk" d>>) goes into a child that has children and asks again from inside, and selects a leaf; `shift+Enter` makes that step a `select`.
